IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g9-interpretation`
IMPORT `g9-common`
IMPORT `g9-sched1-commissioner`

-- g9-tests-sched1.l4: tests of Schedule 1 (g9-sched1-commissioner.l4). Expected values were decided from the text of the Law and the calendar before the module was run. Every threshold is tested on both sides,
-- every date edge on both sides, every route through each list, one case per branch. A DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT, so each regulative rule is run with #TRACE and the outcome it must have is written
-- in the `-- EXPECT:` comment above the trace (checked by check-traces.py): FULFILLED, BREACH, or STANDING (the obligation, permission or prohibition is still open).
-- The clock of a trace is the calendar: AT (DATE_SERIAL day). A deadline written BEFORE a day is met on that day (inclusive).

`A` MEANS `the favoured interpretation`

-- A builder for the appointment records, in the order of the fields: day of the appointment, first day of the term, day the term expires, suitable, views sought on, notice presented on,
-- serving on the day of the appointment, followed by a re-appointment, day became a member of the States, service before.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      first IS A DATE
      expires IS A DATE
      suitable IS A BOOLEAN
      views IS A MAYBE DATE
      notice IS A MAYBE DATE
      serving IS A BOOLEAN
      followed IS A BOOLEAN
      member IS A MAYBE DATE
      service IS A LIST OF `Period of service under the Schedules`
GIVETH AN `Appointment of the Commissioner`
`build an appointment` day first expires suitable views notice serving followed member service MEANS
    `Appointment of the Commissioner` WITH
        `the day of the appointment` IS day
        `the first day of the term` IS first
        `the day the term expires` IS expires
        `the person appears to the Minister to be suitable` IS suitable
        `the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought on` IS views
        `a notice of intention was presented to the States on` IS notice
        `the person was serving as the Commissioner on the day of the appointment` IS serving
        `the term is followed by a re-appointment` IS followed
        `the day on which the person became a member of the States` IS member
        `the service before this appointment` IS service

GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of service under the Schedules`
`no earlier service` MEANS EMPTY

`a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2036-03-01` MEANS `Period of service under the Schedules` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2036 3 1), FALSE
`a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2027-05-01 as a designated person` MEANS `Period of service under the Schedules` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2027 5 1), TRUE
`ten years of service` MEANS LIST `a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2036-03-01`
`a spell as a designated person` MEANS LIST `a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2027-05-01 as a designated person`

-- the appointment of 15 March 2026 for a term from 15 March 2026 to 15 March 2032 (6 years), views sought and notice presented in good time
`the appointment of 2026` MEANS `build an appointment` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2032 3 15) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) FALSE FALSE NOTHING `no earlier service`

§ `Schedule 1: heading`
#CHECK `Sch 1 the heading Jersey Charity Commissioner (inert)`

§ `Schedule 1 paragraph 1: appointment of Commissioner`

§§ `1(1): the Minister must appoint a suitable person`
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
