§§ `1(3): at least 2 weeks before appointing, a notice of intention`
-- the Law's figure is 2 weeks
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention must be presented at least this many weeks before appointing` EQUALS 2
-- appointment on 15 March 2026: the notice on 1 March (14 days before) is in time on reading A and not on reading B (14 clear days: 28 February); 2 March is late on both
`B of F9.1` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.1 is read as B`
`an appointment of 15 March 2026 with a notice on 28 February` MEANS `build an appointment` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2032 3 15) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 2 28)) FALSE FALSE NOTHING `no earlier service`
`an appointment of 15 March 2026 with a notice on 2 March` MEANS `build an appointment` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2032 3 15) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 2)) FALSE FALSE NOTHING `no earlier service`
`an appointment of 15 March 2026 with no notice` MEANS `build an appointment` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2032 3 15) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING `no earlier service`
`an appointment of 15 March 2026 with a notice on 1 March` MEANS `build an appointment` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2032 3 15) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) FALSE FALSE NOTHING `no earlier service`
