§§ `1(5): the period of the appointment, not more than 6 years`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is not more than this many years` EQUALS 6
`B of F9.2` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.2 is read as B`
`an appointment for 6 years to the anniversary` MEANS `build an appointment` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 1) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) FALSE FALSE NOTHING `no earlier service`
`an appointment for 6 years to the day before the anniversary` MEANS `build an appointment` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 2 29) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) FALSE FALSE NOTHING `no earlier service`
`an appointment for 6 years and a day` MEANS `build an appointment` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 2) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) FALSE FALSE NOTHING `no earlier service`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `A` `an appointment for 6 years to the anniversary`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `B of F9.2` `an appointment for 6 years to the anniversary`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `A` `an appointment for 6 years to the day before the anniversary`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `B of F9.2` `an appointment for 6 years to the day before the anniversary`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `A` `an appointment for 6 years and a day`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `B of F9.2` `an appointment for 6 years and a day`
-- a re-appointment for another 6 years is within the limit too (the limit applies to each period of appointment)
`a re-appointment for 6 years` MEANS `build an appointment` (YMD 2032 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 1) (YMD 2038 3 1) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2032 2 1)) (JUST (YMD 2032 2 1)) TRUE FALSE NOTHING `no earlier service`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `A` `a re-appointment for 6 years`
-- the regulative rule: determining a period of 6 years is a performance of the duty; determining one of 6 years and a day is not
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Sch 1 para 1(5) when appointing the Minister must determine the period of the appointment, being not more than 6 years` `A` `an appointment for 6 years to the anniversary` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 1: the Minister determines the period of the appointment` AT 1

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Sch 1 para 1(5) when appointing the Minister must determine the period of the appointment, being not more than 6 years` `A` `an appointment for 6 years and a day` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 1: the Minister determines the period of the appointment` AT 1

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Sch 1 para 1(5) when appointing the Minister must determine the period of the appointment, being not more than 6 years` `B of F9.2` `an appointment for 6 years to the anniversary` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 1: the Minister determines the period of the appointment` AT 1

