§§ `2(4)(a): the remuneration out of the annual income of the States, subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017`
-- trap T22: before 16 December 2019 the text has no carve-out, so the annual income of the States bears the remuneration whatever any Order says; from that text on, an Order that directs the cost to the Fund
-- displaces the States (reading A) or leaves the States liable (reading B). The text before the first consolidated version is not among the sources: a refusal.
`B of F9.9` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.9 is read as B`
